menu "Time Base"

config STM32_TIMEBASE_TIM5_TICK_HZ
    int "TIM5 scheduler tick rate (Hz)"
    range 1 100000
    default 1000
    help
      Rate at which the TIM5 interrupt releases one pass of the slow loop.
      Both timers count microseconds, so the build derives each prescaler from
      the APB1 timer clock and TIM5's period from this rate, and fails when
      either does not come out whole. TIM2 is left free-running as a 32-bit
      microsecond counter and takes no rate of its own.

config STM32_TIMEBASE_TIM5_AUTORELOAD_PRELOAD
    bool "TIM5 auto-reload preload"
    default y
    help
      Buffer TIM5 ARR writes through the preload register so updates take
      effect at the next update event rather than immediately.

endmenu

