config STM32_IMU_GYRO_AAF_DISABLE
    bool "Disable gyro AAF"
    default n
    help
      Disable the gyroscope analog-path anti-alias filter. Default OFF —
      the AAF is the only filter before the ADC, so disabling it lets
      vibration above Nyquist (ODR/2) fold back into the gyro band. Keep
      enabled unless you have a specific reason.

choice
    prompt "Gyro AAF cutoff"
    default STM32_IMU_GYRO_AAF_585HZ
    help
      Anti-alias filter corner for the gyro. The three registers behind it
      (DELT, DELT_SQR, BITSHIFT) are a tabulated triple from datasheet
      section 5.3, not a formula, so the build writes the whole row rather
      than letting the three be set apart. Lower is quieter, higher is
      lower latency; Betaflight's default is 258 Hz and its LOW_LATENCY
      preset is 997 Hz.

config STM32_IMU_GYRO_AAF_258HZ
    bool "258 Hz"

config STM32_IMU_GYRO_AAF_536HZ
    bool "536 Hz"

config STM32_IMU_GYRO_AAF_585HZ
    bool "585 Hz"

config STM32_IMU_GYRO_AAF_997HZ
    bool "997 Hz"

config STM32_IMU_GYRO_AAF_1962HZ
    bool "1962 Hz"

endchoice

config STM32_IMU_ACCEL_AAF_DISABLE
    bool "Disable accel AAF"
    default n
    help
      Disable the accelerometer analog-path anti-alias filter. Default OFF
      — same reasoning as the gyro AAF.

choice
    prompt "Accel AAF cutoff"
    default STM32_IMU_ACCEL_AAF_585HZ
    help
      Anti-alias filter corner for the accelerometer, from the same
      datasheet table as the gyro's. Betaflight pins the accel to 258 Hz
      regardless of the gyro setting.

config STM32_IMU_ACCEL_AAF_258HZ
    bool "258 Hz"

config STM32_IMU_ACCEL_AAF_536HZ
    bool "536 Hz"

config STM32_IMU_ACCEL_AAF_585HZ
    bool "585 Hz"

config STM32_IMU_ACCEL_AAF_997HZ
    bool "997 Hz"

config STM32_IMU_ACCEL_AAF_1962HZ
    bool "1962 Hz"

endchoice

endmenu

menu "FIFO"

config STM32_FAST_LOOP_HZ
    int "Fast control loop rate (Hz)"
    range 1 32000
    default 1000
    help
      Rate at which the attitude and rate controllers run. The FIFO
      watermark interrupt is what drives them, so this sets the watermark
      rather than the other way round: the build computes

        watermark records = record rate / fast loop rate

      where the record rate is the gyro ODR scaled by CLKIN/32000 when the
      external clock is enabled, not the nominal ODR the menu names. A 32768 Hz
      crystal makes a nominal 8 kHz part record at 8192 Hz, so 1024 Hz divides
      evenly and 1000 Hz does not.

      and fails if that is not a whole number, or if those records do not fit
      the 2048-byte FIFO. How many fit depends on the record width, so
      enabling HiRes lowers the ceiling. Raising the gyro ODR keeps this rate
      and reads more records per interrupt.

config STM32_IMU_FIFO_HOLD_LAST
    bool "Hold last FIFO sample"
    default n
    help
      Keep the last sample in the FIFO on overflow instead of dropping all
      buffered data.

config STM32_IMU_FIFO_HIRES_EN
    bool "Enable 20-bit HiRes FIFO (Packet4)"
    default y
    help
      Switch the FIFO from 16-bit Packet3 (16-byte records) to 20-bit
      Packet4 (20-byte records). HiRes mode delivers 18-bit accel + 19-bit
      gyro precision at fixed sensitivities (8192 LSB/g, 131 LSB/dps); the
      FSR setting is forced to ±16g + ±2000 dps internally regardless of
      ACCEL_FS_SEL / GYRO_FS_SEL (datasheet §6.1). Matches PX4 reference
      driver default. Disable for bringup / characterization against
      legacy silicon flashed with older firmware.

endmenu

endmenu

