# Identity reported over MSP on the USB CDC port. A configurator will not admit
# a board exists until it has read this block back, so these are the strings the
# user sees once the port is open — distinct from the USB descriptor strings,
# which only decide whether the port is offered in the first place.

config STM32_MSP_BOARD_IDENTIFIER
    string "Board identifier"
    default "RAVN"
    help
      Four-character board identifier returned by MSP_BOARD_INFO. Shorter
      values are space-padded and longer ones truncated, because the field is
      a fixed four bytes on the wire.

config STM32_MSP_BOARD_NAME
    string "Board name"
    default "32Raven"
    help
      Human-readable board name returned by MSP_BOARD_INFO, shown in the
      configurator's board field.

